Negative control for the page action under a replay (`R6-23`).

Takes the lock off Add new: the collection's own control stays pressable while a
track drives the page, and its tooltip stops naming why it would not fire. The
control keeps its place, its label, its colour and its handoff, and every OTHER
state it has — a declaration's own `disabled`, an action in flight — is
untouched, so the only claim that can go red is the ruled one: a replay is a
PLAYBACK, so the page's own action is held to what the script fires until Live
hands it back, and the refusal SAYS so rather than reading as a dead button.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: page-header.spec.ts — the `R6-23` case (with `locked`, the collection
action is disabled and carries the lock reason).

